defmodule BeamLisp.DecimalOracleTest do
  @moduledoc """
  `BeamLisp.Decimal` against `java.math.BigDecimal`, the reference it models.

  Every row's answer was CAPTURED FROM THE JVM (`clojure -M` evaluating the
  first column with `java.math.BigDecimal`/`RoundingMode` imported) — an
  oracle, not a restatement of this implementation. The second column is the
  beam-lisp spelling of the same computation; the test asserts beam-lisp's
  printed answer equals the JVM's. A row whose JVM side raised
  `ArithmeticException` carries `"ERR"`.

  Coverage: every rounding mode × scale 0/1/2 over 20 values (incl. the
  half-way cases 2.345/2.355/±12.5/0.005), rounded division by 5 divisors ×
  3 modes, exact division (terminating and not), signum/negate/strip/scale/
  precision/longValue/movePointLeft, and a 120-row sample of the pairwise
  add/multiply/compareTo/equals grid (400 pairs each; the full grid is in
  the generator, `/tmp/decor` at the time of writing, and was 0/2580
  divergent modulo one deliberate difference noted in `parse/1`).

  The one KNOWN, DELIBERATE divergence is excluded: `1e3M` reads as scale 0
  here (`1000M`) where the JVM keeps a NEGATIVE scale (`1E+3`, scale −3), so
  products with it print `500` there and `500.0` here. A negative scale is a
  representation detail of BigDecimal that no accounting value needs; this
  type keeps scale ≥ 0 by construction.
  """
  use ExUnit.Case, async: false

  @rows [
    # {jvm expression, beam-lisp expression, JVM answer}
    {"(.toPlainString (.subtract 0M 0.25M))", "(d/plain-str (- 0M 0.25M))", "-0.25"},
    {"(.signum 0M)", "(d/signum 0M)", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.negate 0M))", "(d/plain-str (- 0M))", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.stripTrailingZeros 0M))", "(d/plain-str (d/strip-zeros 0M))", "0"},
    {"(.scale 0M)", "(d/scale 0M)", "0"},
    {"(.precision 0M)", "(d/precision 0M)", "1"},
    {"(.longValue 0M)", "(d/->long 0M)", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.movePointLeft 0M 2))", "(d/plain-str (d/move-point-left 0M 2))", "0.00"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 0 RoundingMode/HALF_EVEN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 0 :half-even))", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 1 RoundingMode/HALF_EVEN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 1 :half-even))", "0.0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 2 RoundingMode/HALF_EVEN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 2 :half-even))", "0.00"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 0 RoundingMode/HALF_UP))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 0 :half-up))", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 1 RoundingMode/HALF_UP))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 1 :half-up))", "0.0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 2 RoundingMode/HALF_UP))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 2 :half-up))", "0.00"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 0 RoundingMode/HALF_DOWN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 0 :half-down))", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 1 RoundingMode/HALF_DOWN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 1 :half-down))", "0.0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 2 RoundingMode/HALF_DOWN))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 2 :half-down))", "0.00"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 0 RoundingMode/CEILING))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 0 :ceiling))", "0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 1 RoundingMode/CEILING))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 1 :ceiling))", "0.0"},
    {"(.toPlainString (.setScale 0M 2 RoundingMode/CEILING))", "(d/plain-str (d/rescale 0M 2 :ceiling))", "0.00"},
